Z||000009||StuGood||12-29-2001||03:12 PM||||The others already posted a pretty good account of the basic procedure.  If you decide to go ahead with the plenum swap, let me recommend one more thing:  use antiseize compound on all the steel bolts that thread into aluminum (including the chrome bolts).  That would be pretty much all of them, of course.  And use a torque wrench.<P>Okay, so that was 2 things  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">.  Stu shut up now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   ||||reg||3
